course: dictionary
lesson: 67
title: The acme: the highest point
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Acme is a noun, and it names the highest point of something: the peak of success, skill or perfection. Look at the clue in «the acme of good manners». The words after of tell you what the peak belongs to, here good manners.
explain: Acme is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in serious writing and old books. Ask yourself what word would fit. In «at the acme of his career», you could say at the very top of his career. That swap shows the meaning.
explain: Acme also works as a company name. In Road Runner cartoons, Wile E. Coyote keeps buying gadgets from ACME, and they always fail. Capital letters often show a name rather than an ordinary word. In «Coyote never catches him, however many ACME rockets he buys», ACME is a brand, not a peak.
fact: The acme of something is its highest point.
fact: Acme is a noun, so you can write the acme.
fact: «The acme of good manners» means the very best good manners.
fact: «At the acme of his career» means at the very top of his work.
fact: ACME is the joke company in Road Runner cartoons, and its gadgets always fail.
exercise: In «the acme of good manners», what does acme mean? | A small, quiet room | A loud noise | *The highest point, the very best | The lowest point of a bad mood
exercise: In the cartoons, what kind of word is ACME? | *A company name, used for a joke business | A sound a coyote makes | A word for a rocket engine | A type of desert animal
exercise: Which phrase means at the very top of his work? | *At the acme of his career | Before the start of his school day | Halfway through the race | Crawling at the bottom of the hill
test: Which word is closest in meaning to acme? | Whisper | Puddle | Basement | *Peak
test: Which sentence uses acme correctly? | We walked the acme of the dog to school. | He wore the acme to bed on Sunday. | The acme of the lunch bell rang loudly. | *She reached the acme of her skill after years of practice.
exam: What does acme mean? | A slow walk | A kind of cloud | *The highest point of something | A small, dusty corner
